* Guided Recovery Pod: motor-driver watchdog
*
* The flight task toggles PET (Heltec GPIO 20) every control cycle while the
* motors may run. Each rising edge pumps charge through C1/D2 into the hold
* capacitor C2. While C2 holds more than about 1.2 V, Q1 conducts, Q1 turns
* Q2 on, and Q2 pulls the DRV8833's SLP (nSLEEP) pin up to 3.3 V: driver
* awake. When the edges stop (pin stuck high, stuck low or floating), C2
* drains through R1/R2, Q1 and Q2 turn off, and R5 pulls SLP low: driver
* asleep, both motors coast. Q3 holds C2 at zero for 50-90 ms after the
* 3.3 V rail comes up, so the rail ramp itself (the pin floats up with the
* rail during boot) cannot wake the driver.
*
* $label

.include $models
.param BFSCALE=$bf ISSCALE=$isscale

* 3.3 V rail from the Heltec, ramping up at power-on
Vcc vcc 0 PWL(0 0 $tramp $vcc)

* The GPIO: an ideal source behind a switch (closed = driving, open = high-Z)
Vsrc petsrc 0 PWL($srcpwl)
Vctl ctl 0 PWL($ctlpwl)
S1 petsrc pet ctl 0 SWPET
Rpull pet $pullnode $rpull

* Charge pump. RA drains C1 when the pin stops toggling high, so a pin stuck
* high trips as fast as one stuck low (D2 keeps it from draining C2).
C1 pet a $c1
D1 0 a DBAT85
D2 a b DBAT85
RA a 0 $ra
C2 b 0 $c2

* Switch: Q1 (NPN) turns Q2 (PNP high side) on
R1 b nb $r1
R2 nb 0 $r2
Q1 n1c nb 0 Q2N3904
R3 n1c nb2 $r3
R4 vcc nb2 $r4
Q2 slp nb2 vcc Q2N3906
R5 slp 0 $r5

* DRV8833 nSLEEP input: 500 kohm internal pulldown, a few pF
Rpd slp 0 500k
Cin slp 0 10p

* Power-on clamp
C3 vcc p $c3
R6 p 0 $r6
R7 p np $r7
Q3 b np 0 Q2N3904

.temp $temp
.options reltol=1e-3 abstol=1e-12 vntol=1e-6 method=gear
.tran $tstep $tstop 0 $tmax
.control
set wr_singlescale
set wr_vecnames
run
wrdata $out v(slp) v(b) v(pet)
quit
.endc
.end
